cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  cogra is an aesthetic, not a research instrument, so there is no need to
  cite it. But if for whatever reason you would like to (a figure that
  looks like 1981 does tend to raise questions), this is how.
title: "Cognitive Revolution Aesthetic (cogra)"
abstract: >-
  The look of experimental psychology journals from the cognitive revolution
  for figures and papers: a matplotlib style and ggplot2-style geoms in
  black ink, archival-scan wear, papers set as a 1980 journal article,
  and extras for R, LaTeX and the web.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lynde
    family-names: Wolf Gorneault
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4484-5120"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lynde-wolf/cogra"
keywords:
  - matplotlib
  - data visualization
  - typography
  - psychology
  - cognitive revolution
